.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-service-autoscale - Autoscaling / alert threshold of a service


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container service autoscale   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Autoscaling / alert threshold of a service

.PP
Body \fB{"autoscaling": {"enabled": true, "min": 1, "max": 5, "cpu_percent": 70, "memory_percent": 0}, "alerts": {"min_ready": 2}}\fR\&. Replicas are added when the average use exceeds the target (at most double per 30 s) and removed one per minute after 3 calm minutes. Max cannot exceed the plan replica limit; replicas that do not fit in the node pool wait (\fBwarnings: max_exceeds_capacity\fR, alert \fBcapacity\fR). Not a revision. Switching off keeps the current replica count (or \fBreplicas\fR).

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/containers/{id}/services/{name}/autoscaling (operationId typed_put_containers\fBid\fPservices\fBname\fPautoscaling, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--alerts\fP=""
	Alert threshold: notify when fewer replicas are ready (0 = off). Channels: PUT /cloud/containers/{id}/notifications. (JSON)

.PP
\fB--autoscaling\fP=""
	Autoscaling (horizontal): replicas follow the average CPU (and optionally memory) use of the reserved size. \fBenabled:false\fR = off (fixed replicas). (JSON)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for autoscale

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--replicas\fP=0
	Fixed replicas when switching autoscaling off

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)


